# System, privilege, and targets

## Agent freedom on this machine

- This repo is a **workstation setup / desktop platform**. The agent may run **real applies**, including root, `dnf`, `systemctl`, greeter/session installs, and live MDE binary swaps when that verifies or advances the work.
- Prefer real verification over dry-run theater when the change is meant to land on this seat.
- Still avoid irreversible data loss (wiping unrelated user data, rewriting disk partitions) unless explicitly requested.

## Privilege model

- **Setup / install path:** root and polkit are OK (`mde/install.sh`, package installs, greetd/seatd, system units).
- **Runtime session:** keep the daily-driver session **unprivileged**. Privileged helpers (`mde-privileged`, PAM unlock, polkit actions) stay narrow and intentional.
- Do not broaden privileged attack surface “for convenience” in session chrome; put elevation behind explicit user actions or install-time configuration.

## Targets

- Primary: **latest Fedora stable** and **linux-surface** where relevant.
- Develop and test assuming x86_64 Wayland MDE on this class of hardware.
- Keep installer handoff compatible with minimal/server → MDE, but do not sacrifice MDE quality for parity with every alternate DE.

## Assets and branding

- Free to update brand, theme, icon, and related assets under `assets/` and `mde/assets/` when UI work needs it.
- Windows-adjacent density and metaphors (taskbar height, flyouts, Start, Settings) beat stock GNOME/libadwaita defaults when choosing UI behavior.
- When replacing icons/fonts/themes, prefer assets that keep Mackes/MDE look coherent with the live shell.

## Catalog and flags

- Package lists in `catalog/` and installer feature flags must stay consistent with what MDE/install actually needs.
- Any feature that requires packages: update **catalog + installer flags + MDE install handoff** together.
